                <pb facs="0750" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/98: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt
                        to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName type="venue">U. S. S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Potomac</hi>,”</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1937-12-02T00:00:00">December 2 [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">1?</hi>], 1937—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        December 2—1:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Entirely approve your recommendations about possible declaration. Please see
                    Secretary of Treasury at once about his telegram to me about silver and
                    exchange. I am inclined to go along with his suggestions.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin</hi> D. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
